      <div type="clause" n="60">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 60</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="60" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="116" ed="#liebermann"/>CIIII. Se ceorl se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.17-2"/> ðe hæfð oðres geoht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.18"/> ahyrod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.19"/>, gif he hæbbe ealle on foðre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.20"/> to agifanne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.13"/>, gesceawige mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.21"/>, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.13"/> ealle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.22"/>; gif he næbbe, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.13"/> healf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.23"/> on fodre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.20"/>, healfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.24"/> on oþru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="60" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="116" ed="#liebermann"/>CIIII. Se ciorl þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.3"/> hæbbe oðres geoht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.4-2"/> ahyred, gif he hæbbe ealle on foðre to agyfanne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.2"/>, gesceawige mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.5"/>; gif he næbbe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.6"/>, agife healf on foðre, healf on oþrum ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="60" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="116" ed="#liebermann"/>Be hyroxan. Se ceorl se ðe hæfð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.4"/> oðres oxan ahýred, gyf he hæbbe ealle on foðre to agyfanne, gesceawige mon, agyfe ealle; gyf he næbbe, agyfe healf on foðre, healf on oðrum ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="60" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="117" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.14"/> uillanus alterius boues<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.15"/> locauerit, si totum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.16"/> habeat in annona persoluere, uideatur hoc, et reddat; si non habeat, reddat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_60.lnote.oe.17"/> dimidium in annona, dimidium in alio captali.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="56" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be hyroxan.] Se ceorl se ðe hæfð<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_60.attnote.fn.10"/> oðres geoht<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_60.attnote.fn.11"/> ahyrod, gif he hæbbe ealle on foðre to agifanne, gesceawige mon, agife ealle; gif he næbbe, agife healf on fodre, healfe on oþrum ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="64" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="422" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{CIIII} Se ceorl se ðe hæfð oðres geoht ahyrod, gif he hæbbe ealle on forðre to agifanne, gesceawege mon, agife ealle. Gif he næbbe, agife healf on fodre, healfe on oþru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="117" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn der Bauer, welcher eines anderen Joch [Rinder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_60.lnote.de.1"/>] gemiethet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_60.lnote.de.2"/> hat, [die Miethe] ganz in Futter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_60.lnote.de.3"/> zu zahlen hat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_60.lnote.de.4"/>, sehe man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_60.lnote.de.5"/> zu, [dass er] sie ganz zahle; wenn er [das] nicht hat, zahle er halb in Futter, halb in anderem Werthe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If the peasant who has hired another’s yoke [of oxen] has [the rent] to pay entirely in fodder, let it be seen to [that he] pays it in full; if he does not have [it], let him pay half in fodder, half in other goods.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="57" ed="#attenborough"/>If a commoner, who has hired another's yoke of oxen, is able to pay all the hire in fodder, care should be taken that he does pay it all [in this form]. If he is not able to do so, he shall pay half [the hire] in fodder, and half in other goods.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="406" ed="#whitelock"/>The <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> who has hired another’s yoke [of oxen], if he has enough to pay for it entirely in fodder—let one see that he pays in full; if he has not, he is to pay half in fodder, half in other goods.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="423" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>A <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> who has hired another’s yoke, if he is able to pay it all in fodder, make sure he gives all. If he cannot, let him pay half in fodder and half in other goods.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_60.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">116</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> hæfh</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from hæfh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_60.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">117</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Cap.</hi> 60. 61 <hi rend="italic">fehlen Lond; am Rande [aus T?] Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cap. 60. 61 lacking in Lond; in the margin [from T?] Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_60.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">117</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">boue <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">boue R</seg></note>
